   {
    "code": "occupancy_not_stored",
    "severity": "warning",
    "message": "Of 91063 occupancy entries MetaMorpheus wrote, some are not in ptm_stoichiometry: 7596 site not in ptm_sites. 'site not in ptm_sites' means the entry's site has no ptm_sites row to key on; 'not determinable' means a cell's segments could not be assigned to its accessions from the sequences (QuantProject DEF-OCC-ACCESSION), which is never guessed. Absence of a row for these sites is therefore not NA. A 'duplicate' is a second entry for a (site, run) that already has a row: one with identical values loses nothing; one with DIFFERENT values means MetaMorpheus wrote two answers and the first in file order was stored (examples in bundle.json occupancy.differing_duplicates; which one should be stored is QuantProject's to define)."
   },
   {
    "code": "peptide_rows_localization_ambiguous",
    "severity": "warning",
    "message": "646 row(s) of AllQuantifiedPeptides.tsv name several full sequences, joined by `|`: a peptide whose modification site the search did not settle (MetaMorpheus #2917). Their 2016 value(s) are not stored, since storing them under one of the sequences would place them on a site the search never decided. The PSMs behind them are in `psms`. E.g. `AAPSVTLFPPSSEELQAN[Common Artifact:Deamidation on N]KATLVC[Common Fixed:Carbamidomethyl on C]LISDFYPGAVTVAWKADSSPVK|AAPSVTLFPPSSEELQ[Common Artifact:Deamidation on Q]ANKATLVC[Common Fixed:Carbamidomethyl on C]LISDFYPGAVTVAWKADSSPVK`, `AAVAASGLNTMLEGNGQ[Common Artifact:Deamidation on Q]YTLLAPTNEAFEKIPSETLNR|AAVAASGLNTMLEGN[Common Artifact:Deamidation on N]GQYTLLAPTNEAFEKIPSETLNR`, `AAVAASGLNTMLEGNGQ[Common Artifact:Deamidation on Q]YTLLAPTNEAFEK|AAVAASGLNTMLEGN[Common Artifact:Deamidation on N]GQYTLLAPTNEAFEK`."
   },
   {
    "code": "sdrf_uncoded",
    "severity": "warning",
    "message": "The deposited SDRF describes its samples only as text with no ontology term, so the curated organism part, cell type, disease and individual columns are empty. The text is in sample_characteristics: disease: control, exfoliation glaucoma, exfoliation syndrome; organism part: lens capsule, trabecular meshwork or iris (runs 43-48), trabecular meshwork or iris (runs 88-93). Match on it as text; it has not been mapped to a term."
   },
   {
    "code": "unplaced_ptm_sites",
    "severity": "warning",
    "message": "Some modifications on peptides shared between proteins were not written to ptm_sites for one or more of those proteins, because the peptide could not be located in that protein's sequence and the producer's residue spans cannot be paired with its accessions. Of the (PSM, protein) pairs affected: 569 named a protein that does not contain the stored peptide -- typically a PSM ambiguous between peptide sequences (level 4 or 5), where this protein carries a different candidate than the first, which is the one stored. Sites on the other proteins of the same PSMs are written. Counts are in bundle.json under protein_databases."
   },
   {
    "code": "unresolved_modifications",
    "severity": "warning",
    "message": "1 modification(s) could not be mapped to a UNIMOD accession or a mass, and are carried in ProForma as [Info:...] tags: UniProt:S-(15-deoxy-Delta12,14-prostaglandin J2-9-yl)cysteine on C. Their ptm_sites rows exist and carry modification_name, with modification null, so a query by name finds them and a query by UNIMOD accession will not."
   },
   {
    "code": "occupancy_decoy_groups",
    "severity": "info",
    "message": "65 occupancy entries on decoy protein groups were not stored: MetaMorpheus computes them, and they are FDR machinery, not biology."
   },
   {
    "code": "run_counts_missing",
    "severity": "info",
    "message": "No per-run `metrics` row from results.txt for `psms_1pct` (21 of 21 runs), `peptides` (21 of 21 runs), `protein_groups` (21 of 21 runs). These counts were not written, which is not a count of zero. The search task sets `WriteIndividualFiles = false`, and MetaMorpheus writes results.txt's per-file PSM, peptide and protein-group lines only when it is true (before 1.1.14, MetaMorpheus #2955, its per-file precursor and MS2 lines too). PXReprise's QC payload counts each run's share of the whole search's 1% set instead, a different number (the FDR is the whole search's, not recomputed on each file), under names of its own (`source = 'qc_payload.json'`): `psms_1pct_whole_search` for 21 of the 21 runs, `peptides_1pct_whole_search` for 21 of the 21 runs, `protein_groups_1pct_whole_search` for 21 of the 21 runs."
   }
